# One text of a class is evaluated twice. Compiled code tells the private names of the two evaluations apart by the token of each; the text of a direct eval asked by the symbol of the key, which is one for both: `#weigh in other` was true for an object of the other evaluation, its field was read and stored, its method and accessors ran. A text is handed the symbols of its own evaluation; a compiled object answers them by its brand.
